  "policies": [
    "Daze returns the actual enemy minion to its original owner through the ordinary physical return/death path. Only a successful arrival receives the existing hand lock before any return reaction. Its immediately active lock spans the next genuine owner start and expires on the following owner start (two starts); extra turns count, skipped slots do not. Returning a stolen original caster-owned minion and the current-turn reach of the marker remain M6 policy.",
    "Cursed Chains binds the previous controller and that original player's genuine turn-ended deadline, separately from its current-global-turn attack prohibition. Transfer, return marker and attack policy are installed before reactions. Existing silence, transform, reset, death, copy and failed full-board return policies remain; overlapping temporary control sources still explicitly reject and remain a real incomplete card interaction, not complete CN support.",
    "Hatching Ceremony installs the public objective and buffs the then-current active friendly minions through existing captured batch recipients. Next-owner-turn-end duration counts the current owner end only if installation precedes its captured end boundary; off-turn and end-reaction installations therefore start at one remaining end, ordinary owner main-phase installations at two. Source lifecycle, duplicate instances, slot capacity, choice restoration and group notification policies remain shared.",
    "Sigil of the Seas installs the existing one-owner-start sigil and requests the exact officially linked 3/3 Taunt Naga through attributed card summoning. No extra executable proxy or enchantment card is invented.",
    "Root registration and internal validation are separate from complete Standard membership, hotfix and CN timing evidence. CATA_581 formula, full generators and all remaining roots/reachable content stay open."
  ]
